-- ============================================================
-- Alonecraft -- passive-to-active talent redesigns: unhide the icon
-- ============================================================
--
-- BUG: "Sacrifice the Weak doesn't appear in my spellbook despite having
--      it in my talents."
--
-- Every talent that woa_2026_08_01_* turned from a passive into an ACTIVE
-- ability cleared SPELL_ATTR0_PASSIVE (0x40) from the inherited Attributes
-- value but left the rest of the bitmask alone:
--
--   464 (0x1D0) - 0x40 = 400 (0x190)
--                        = 0x100 DO_NOT_LOG
--                        | 0x080 DO_NOT_DISPLAY   <-- the problem
--                        | 0x010 IS_ABILITY
--
-- SharedDefines.h:377 -- SPELL_ATTR0_DO_NOT_DISPLAY: "Not visible in
-- spellbook or aura bar (Spellbook, Aura Icon, Combat Log)".  Blizzard set
-- it because the spell used to be a passive talent rank that the client
-- must never draw; on an active ability it hides the button.
--
-- 400 -> 272 (0x110) keeps DO_NOT_LOG and IS_ABILITY, drops DO_NOT_DISPLAY.
--
-- Applied to every redesign of this shape, since they all inherited the
-- same value: Sacrifice the Weak (47220), Infernal Bargain (63349) and
-- Bone Shield (200119).  Syncretism (200094, Attributes 448) is left
-- alone -- it is still genuinely passive (0x40 set).  Infernal Bargain
-- ranks 2 and 3 are not touched here: woa_2026_08_03_12.sql collapses
-- that talent to a single rank and drops their overrides entirely.
--
-- NOTE: this is only half the fix.  The talent also needs
-- Talent.dbc.Flags = 1 (addToSpellBook) on the SERVER's copy of Talent.dbc
-- -- Player.cpp:14187 will not call learnSpell() without it -- and
-- build_and_run.bat only ever deployed the patched Spell.dbc to
-- C:\Build\...\Data\dbc.  Talent.dbc deployment is added there in the same
-- change as this file.
--
-- ============================================================


-- ============================================================
-- Sacrifice the Weak: clear SPELL_ATTR0_DO_NOT_DISPLAY (0x80)
-- ============================================================
